% Filter profiles compose named allow-lists via a small parent DAG,
% mirroring the lecture-mode graph in the core package, but with
% union-of-ancestors closure instead of single-selection: a profile that
% has both a "solutions" and a "grading" profile as parents keeps
% everything either parent keeps. A leaf lecture-mode selects at most one
% filter profile (\cs{AssignLtxtalkFilterProfile}); once one is selected,
% its closed allow-list is merged into the baseline (commands and
% environments declared without \code{profile=}, which stay in effect no
% matter which, if any, profile applies) the first time the scanner
% engages. Modes that select no profile keep exactly the previously
% existing \code{ignorenonframetext} behavior.
\seq_new:N  \g_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_profile_known_seq
\prop_new:N \g_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_profile_parents_prop
\bool_new:N \g_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_profile_frozen_bool
\prop_new:N \g_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_mode_profile_prop
\tl_new:N   \l_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_selected_profile_tl
\bool_new:N \g_osglecture_modes_ltxtalk_profile_resolved_bool
